.TH OMACHATD 8 "2026-08-31" "OmaChat 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
omachatd \- per-user OmaChat daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachatd
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB--state\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB--anchors\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB--file-key\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Owns identities, sealed state, the Nostr transport, and the versioned IPC
socket.
Only the Nostr transport is currently wired into the daemon; the mesh transport
is not yet integrated.
SIGHUP validates a replacement configuration before applying it.
SIGINT stops cleanly.
.SH ACCOUNT
The JSON configuration may set account_handle and account_display_name. These
values are sealed into a root-signed local account binding and survive restart.
A configured handle is reported as local-only until a signed central-registry
receipt proves global uniqueness. The separate nickname setting remains the
public geohash-chat nickname and is never populated from the account handle.
.SH PRIVATE RELAYS
The optional dm_relays JSON array enables the standard NIP-17 private inbox.
The optional geo_relays object enables separate pinned per-geohash pools.
Its mode is supplement (default) or replace, and overrides is an array of
at most ten WSS URLs (numeric-loopback WS is allowed for tests).
Replace requires a nonempty override list. At most eight cells and ten relays
per cell are supported. Failed candidates are re-evaluated every 30 seconds
and become eligible again after five minutes. Status includes profile and
snapshot hashes plus selected/skipped endpoints. Policy changes require restart.
Each ws or wss relay must authenticate the persisted device Nostr principal
with NIP-42 before receiving its recipient-only kind-1059 subscription. An
empty array disables this inbox. Relay changes require a daemon restart. A
configured relay provides reachability and is not treated as protocol authority.
.SH ROOMS
The optional rooms JSON object enables standard NIP-29 rooms: rooms.relays lists
room relays and rooms.anchor_directory optionally places the room-state
generation anchors. Each relay is bound to the signing identity its NIP-11
document declares, and rooms are addressed as room:RELAY_PUBKEY:GROUP so the
same group ID under another relay key is a different room. Membership is the
relay's policy decision; the daemon only subscribes and sends join, leave, and
message events signed by the device Nostr identity. Room state is sealed per
relay identity and its generation is anchored outside the state directory
(--anchors, default <state>-anchors) so a state directory restored from backup
is refused instead of silently rewound. Relay changes require a daemon restart.
.SH STORAGE
Secret Service is preferred. --file-key selects a 0600 master key in the
0700 state directory. A missing selected key is fatal; it is never silently
regenerated.
.SH SYSTEMD
Start with "systemctl --user enable --now omachatd.service". To keep a powered,
awake machine serving after logout, the owner may explicitly run
"loginctl enable-linger $USER"; reverse with "loginctl disable-linger $USER".
Suspend, power loss, radio loss, and network loss interrupt service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omachat (1),
.BR omachat-ctl (1),
.BR omachat-protocol (7)
